 Cached JPEG data may occupy at most 12 GiB. Before admitting a completed sheet, evict enough existing sheets to remain within that bound. Temporary render output is kept separately and removed on completion or failure. Eviction never deletes source footage or changes job-ticket semantics.
 
-The eviction policy is still open. Candidates are LRU, frequency-based eviction with aging, and 2Q. LRU has little bookkeeping and follows recent work quickly but is vulnerable to sequential scans. Aged frequency counts protect repeatedly popular clips but add counter maintenance and can lag a project switch. 2Q separates first-use entries from reused entries, resisting scans at the cost of extra queues and a queue-size parameter. None changes the external interface, queue concurrency, or disk budget.
+### 2Q Eviction Policy
+
+The worker partitions replacement tracking into three private queues while keeping the 12 GiB on-disk JPEG budget, external HTTP contract, and render-queue concurrency unchanged:
+
+- **A1in (FIFO admission queue)**: Holds newly rendered sheets on first admission. Hits in A1in return the cached JPEG without moving the entry out of A1in.
+- **A1out (FIFO ghost queue)**: Holds metadata keys only (no JPEG bytes on disk) for sheets recently evicted from A1in. Bounded by entry count so ghost metadata remains small.
+- **Am (LRU main queue)**: Holds reused sheets. Hits in Am refresh the entry to the most-recently-used position.
+
+On a cache miss, if the key is absent from A1out, the completed sheet is admitted to A1in; if the key is present in A1out, it is removed from A1out and the completed sheet is admitted directly to Am. When A1in exceeds its byte budget, the oldest entry's JPEG is deleted and its key is appended to A1out (evicting the oldest ghost key if A1out is at capacity). When Am exceeds its byte budget, the least-recently-used entry's JPEG is deleted. Initial queue-size parameters default to a 25% / 75% byte split between A1in (3 GiB) and Am (9 GiB), with A1out sized to track keys for up to 50% of nominal sheet capacity.
+
+## Decisions & Alternatives
+
+| Decision | Chosen | Alternatives Considered | Rationale |
+|----------|--------|------------------------|-----------|
+| Cache eviction policy | 2Q (A1in FIFO, A1out ghost FIFO, Am LRU) | LRU; frequency-based eviction with aging | Protects repeatedly compared sheets from eviction during long sequential screenings without the stale-retention lag of aged frequency counters; all queue bookkeeping stays private to the preview worker. |
+
